Case ID: GPO-043
Reason for Visit: Acute psychological distress and extreme anxiety related to an immediate, mandatory administrative deadline for a critical, life-saving specialist appointment tomorrow morning.
Location: Private residence
Present at Visit: Patient only
Urgency Justification: Telephone triage reported an elderly patient with severe, complex oncology needs who realized their mandatory specialist referral had expired. The patient has a critical, non-reschedulable chemotherapy review at 0800 hours tomorrow morning, and the specialist clinic absolutely mandates a valid referral to proceed with the infusion. Urgent face-to-face assessment was strictly required to conduct a brief clinical assessment, verify clinical stability, and immediately generate the legal referral document to prevent the catastrophic cancellation of the patient's oncology treatment. Delaying this assessment would have resulted in a dangerous lapse in life-saving care.

