Risk Level: Environmental/Social Risk: Low (High clinical risk if treatment delayed)

CLINICAL REASONING SUMMARY
The patient experienced a severe acute stress reaction entirely driven by a critical, impending administrative barrier to their life-saving oncology treatment. Telephone triage correctly identified that the patient's treatment would be dangerously interrupted without immediate medical intervention. Urgent face-to-face assessment was mandated to quickly confirm the patient's physiological stability, rule out any acute complications from the chemotherapy, and immediately draft the mandatory legal referral document. By providing the physical referral on-site, the absolute trigger for the patient's panic was neutralized, securing their chemotherapy appointment tomorrow morning and preventing a severe, unwarranted psychological crisis.

