Clinical Interventions: Conducted a brief, targeted physical examination to confirm baseline clinical stability. Drafted and signed an updated, comprehensive 12-month specialist referral letter detailing the interval history and current medications. Provided a physical copy to the patient and faxed a copy directly to the oncology clinic.
Positive Behavioral Change: To absolutely prevent this severe administrative stress from ever happening again, permanently write the exact expiration date of this new 12-month referral in bright red marker on the front cover of your main medical folder tonight. Set a calendar reminder in your phone for 11 months from today. By creating a loud, unavoidable visual cue on your most frequently used medical item, you force an administrative check long before a crisis deadline approaches.
Home-Based Services (Optional): None indicated.
DME/Safety (Optional): None.
Follow-up: No acute GP follow-up required; patient to attend oncology appointment tomorrow morning.

